# What `docker build` never sends from workers/ — the build context of the
# Python worker's image (workers/Dockerfile.worker), which copies app/ whole.
# The worker runs model tool calls on user-supplied URLs, so a secret left in
# its image is the one most worth keeping out. Its settings arrive as the
# container's environment at run time; nothing here is read at build time.
# scripts/check_image_contents.sh in the template repository plants each of
# these and fails if any reaches an image.

# Secrets. Every env file at any depth, .env.example included.
**/.env*
**/.vault-pass
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Dependencies and environments. Poetry installs the worker's from
# poetry.lock; db-writer, also under here, has its own image and context.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv

# Python and test artefacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/coverage
**/.coverage
**/*.log
